# for (i = start; i < 10; ..) s[i], with `start` a value of which a number is only expected, and a cast on the key: flow has seen that nothing with a fraction arrives.
# The site of the read is planned with the type of that operand, so its tests promise a key without a fraction. The comparison in front has tested the value in front of the cast for `number`,
# and what that test lets through stands for the key in every test behind it. Of that value only `number` is proven, so the presence test promises nothing about fractions.
# The read gets the cast in front of it again and keeps the promise
# FORM: Prepared optimizing
# RUN: pass PlaceTypeTests VerifyProgram

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="readsAtCastKey" parameters=[{type=Array<number>}, {type=number flags=[IsExpected]}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: Array<number>, v1: anything ~ number):
    v2 = Integer integer=10
    v3 = Less v1, v2
    Branch v3 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b1():
    v4 = AssumeType v1 provenType=undefined|int|whole
    v5 = ElemGet v0, v4
    v6 = Check v5 expectedType=number
    Return v6
  b2():
    Return v2
# CHECK: = TypeTest v1 testedType=number
# CHECK: [[key]]: int|whole = AssumeType [[number]], [[here22]] provenType=undefined|int|whole
